{'global_id': 'medeasi_000088', 'source_text': 'Children usually outgrow these manifestations and react increasingly to inhaled allergens, with symptoms of asthma and rhinitis; this progression is called atopic march. By age 10 years, patients rarely have respiratory symptoms after the allergenic food is eaten, even though skin tests remain positive.', 'source_metrics': {'FRE': 32.22, 'ARI': 17.5, 'FKGL': 14.2, 'Dale-Chall': 12.26, 'char_count': 304, 'alphanum_count': 253, 'word_count': 50, 'sentence_count': 2}, 'metadata': {'dataset': 'medeasi', 'experiment_split': '', 'domain': 'medical', 'language': 'en', 'annotation': 'human', 'level': 'sentence'}, 'simplification_text': 'By about age 1 year, the rash tends to develop less often, but children may start to react to inhaled allergens (such as pollen) and have asthma symptoms. They may wheeze, feel short of breath, or get a runny nose when they eat the food that triggers their allergy. By about age 10, children rarely have asthma symptoms after the food is eaten.', 'target_metrics': {'FRE': 67.08, 'ARI': 10.2, 'FKGL': 9.1, 'Dale-Chall': 8.69, 'char_count': 344, 'alphanum_count': 269, 'word_count': 73, 'sentence_count': 3, 'char_compression_rate': 1.13, 'word_compression_rate': 1.46, 'sentence_compression_rate': 1.5, 'BLEU': 5.934488823020527, 'BERTScore': 0.8927241563796997}, 'simplification_version': 1, 'grade_level': -1, 'simplification_dimensions': {'linguistic': {'lexical': False, 'syntactic': False}}}
