{'global_id': 'medeasi_001181', 'source_text': 'Nansen studied zoology at the Royal Frederick University in Christiania ( renamed Oslo in 1925 ), and later worked as a curator at the Bergen Museum where his research on the central nervous system of lower marine creatures earned him a doctorate and helped establish modern theories of neurology.', 'source_metrics': {'FRE': 6.85, 'ARI': 27.0, 'FKGL': 24.0, 'Dale-Chall': 15.37, 'char_count': 297, 'alphanum_count': 241, 'word_count': 51, 'sentence_count': 1}, 'metadata': {'dataset': 'medeasi', 'experiment_split': '', 'domain': 'medical', 'language': 'en', 'annotation': 'human', 'level': 'sentence'}, 'simplification_text': 'Nansen studied zoology at the Royal Frederick University, and later worked as a curator at the Bergen Museum where his research on the central nervous system of lower marine creatures earned him a doctorate and helped establish modern theories of neurology.\n', 'target_metrics': {'FRE': 12.94, 'ARI': 24.0, 'FKGL': 21.6, 'Dale-Chall': 14.91, 'char_count': 258, 'alphanum_count': 215, 'word_count': 43, 'sentence_count': 1, 'char_compression_rate': 0.87, 'word_compression_rate': 0.84, 'sentence_compression_rate': 1.0, 'BLEU': 79.92640677297831, 'BERTScore': 0.9746861457824707}, 'simplification_version': 1, 'grade_level': -1, 'simplification_dimensions': {'linguistic': {'lexical': False, 'syntactic': False}}}
