{'global_id': 'medeasi_001688', 'source_text': 'The clitoris, vestibular bulbs, labia minora, and urethra consist of two histologically distinct types of vascular tissue, the first of which is trabeculated, erectile tissue present in the clitoris and the bulbs, which have large, dilated vascular spaces filled with blood and are spongy in appearance.', 'source_metrics': {'FRE': 7.87, 'ARI': 28.0, 'FKGL': 23.6, 'Dale-Chall': 12.44, 'char_count': 303, 'alphanum_count': 250, 'word_count': 54, 'sentence_count': 1}, 'metadata': {'dataset': 'medeasi', 'experiment_split': '', 'domain': 'medical', 'language': 'en', 'annotation': 'human', 'level': 'sentence'}, 'simplification_text': 'In both the clitoris and the penis, there are two types of erectile tissue.', 'target_metrics': {'FRE': 74.19, 'ARI': 6.4, 'FKGL': 6.4, 'Dale-Chall': 9.97, 'char_count': 75, 'alphanum_count': 60, 'word_count': 16, 'sentence_count': 1, 'char_compression_rate': 0.25, 'word_compression_rate': 0.3, 'sentence_compression_rate': 1.0, 'BLEU': 2.1294883063040193, 'BERTScore': 0.8754559755325317}, 'simplification_version': 1, 'grade_level': -1, 'simplification_dimensions': {'linguistic': {'lexical': False, 'syntactic': False}}}
