{'global_id': 'medeasi_001823', 'source_text': 'It is generally accepted that there exist three mechanisms responsible for (apparently) random behavior in systems: Randomness coming from the environment (for example, Brownian motion, but also hardware random number generators) Randomness coming from the initial conditions.', 'source_metrics': {'FRE': -16.85, 'ARI': 27.6, 'FKGL': 24.8, 'Dale-Chall': 12.73, 'char_count': 276, 'alphanum_count': 232, 'word_count': 45, 'sentence_count': 1}, 'metadata': {'dataset': 'medeasi', 'experiment_split': '', 'domain': 'medical', 'language': 'en', 'annotation': 'human', 'level': 'sentence'}, 'simplification_text': 'There are several ways in which a process or system can be seen as random: Randomness coming from the environment (for example, Brownian motion, but also hardware random number generators).', 'target_metrics': {'FRE': 32.57, 'ARI': 18.7, 'FKGL': 16.2, 'Dale-Chall': 10.39, 'char_count': 189, 'alphanum_count': 154, 'word_count': 36, 'sentence_count': 1, 'char_compression_rate': 0.68, 'word_compression_rate': 0.8, 'sentence_compression_rate': 1.0, 'BLEU': 43.19030240752368, 'BERTScore': 0.9314358234405518}, 'simplification_version': 1, 'grade_level': -1, 'simplification_dimensions': {'linguistic': {'lexical': False, 'syntactic': False}}}
