{'global_id': 'medeasi_000487', 'source_text': 'Tonsillopharyngitis is usually viral, most often caused by the common cold viruses (adenovirus, rhinovirus, influenza, coronavirus, and respiratory syncytial virus), but occasionally by Epstein-Barr virus, herpes simplex virus, cytomegalovirus, or HIV.', 'source_metrics': {'FRE': -36.14, 'ARI': 27.8, 'FKGL': 26.0, 'Dale-Chall': 15.36, 'char_count': 252, 'alphanum_count': 209, 'word_count': 43, 'sentence_count': 1}, 'metadata': {'dataset': 'medeasi', 'experiment_split': '', 'domain': 'medical', 'language': 'en', 'annotation': 'human', 'level': 'sentence'}, 'simplification_text': 'Tonsillopharyngitis is usually caused by a virus. Most often, it is one of the viruses that cause the common cold, such as rhinovirus, adenovirus, influenza virus, or respiratory syncytial virus. Less often, another virus is involved, such as the Epstein-Barr virus (which causes mononucleosis) or human immunodeficiency virus (HIV).', 'target_metrics': {'FRE': 21.09, 'ARI': 14.1, 'FKGL': 14.4, 'Dale-Chall': 10.57, 'char_count': 333, 'alphanum_count': 270, 'word_count': 63, 'sentence_count': 3, 'char_compression_rate': 1.32, 'word_compression_rate': 1.47, 'sentence_compression_rate': 3.0, 'BLEU': 8.063911358699183, 'BERTScore': 0.9204116463661194}, 'simplification_version': 1, 'grade_level': -1, 'simplification_dimensions': {'linguistic': {'lexical': False, 'syntactic': False}}}
